  "body": "## Goal\n\nAdd Hermes as a separate source adapter for the coding-agent usage dashboard.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Discover the local Hermes session/tool logs or session DB available on this machine.\n- Extract trustworthy Hermes usage fields where available:\n  - session id\n  - timestamp\n  - title or session summary\n  - provider/model\n  - input tokens\n  - output tokens\n  - cache read/write tokens, if available\n- Normalize Hermes records into the shared dashboard record shape:\n\n```text\ntool, session_id, timestamp, title, provider, model, input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read, cache_write\n```\n\n## UI behavior\n\n- Add Hermes to the tool filter once Hermes records are available.\n- Show Hermes rows in overview cards, daily chart, model breakdown, and usage history.\n- Keep OpenCode-only behavior unchanged when Hermes data is missing.\n- If Hermes data exists but some metrics are unavailable, show that explicitly instead of silently treating missing values as zero.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Do not add Codex support in this issue; track Codex separately.\n- Do not claim cost parity unless pricing/model IDs can be matched reliably.\n- Do not infer unavailable token counts from message text.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Dashboard loads with OpenCode-only data exactly as before.\n- Dashboard loads with Hermes data when local Hermes records are present.\n- Missing Hermes data is shown as unavailable, not as zero usage.\n- Validation documents the Hermes source path(s), schema/format, and which metrics are trustworthy.\n- Chart and table ordering remain consistent: same top-N order, same position colors, Other muted gray.\n\nPart of #1.\n",
